Abstract = {Isoprene (C5H8) is the non-methane hydrocarbon with the highest
   emissions to the atmosphere. It is mainly produced by vegetation,
   especially broad-leaved trees, and efficiently transported to the upper
   troposphere in deep convective clouds, where it is mixed with lightning
   NOx. Isoprene oxidation products drive rapid formation and growth of new
   particles in the tropical upper troposphere. However, isoprene oxidation
   pathways at low temperatures are not well understood. Here, in
   experiments at the CERN CLOUD chamber at 223 K and 243 K, we find that
   isoprene oxygenated organic molecules (IP-OOM) all involve two
