Year = {2008},
Volume = {3},
Number = {3},
Month = {JUL-SEP},
Abstract = {The comprehensive model MAID (model for aerosol and ice dynamics) was
   developed to simulate condensation and freezing in aerosol particles
   residing in the UT/LS (upper troposphere/lower stratosphere). The exact
   balancing of trace gas components is a particular emphasis of MAID. MAID
   is applied to and verified by experiments in the aerosol chamber AIDA,
   and, moreover, it is adapted to Lagrangian atmospheric cirrus cloud
   simulations. Here, the model is introduced, and as an example for model
   applications the significant influence of homogeneous or heterogeneous
   freezing on ice cloud microphysics and the water and nitric acid
   partitioning in cirrus clouds is shown.},
